body: "The `release` job of the Daily Release workflow failed.\n\n- Failing job: `release`\n- Run URL: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/actions/runs/33081605178\n- Commit: f519a48843ca9e363475ee5852fb27fcd0157af1\n- Date (UTC): 2026-08-27T14:29:37Z\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-09-01T04:51:40Z)\n>\n> Closing as resolved and stale.\n> \n> This issue was filed automatically while npm publishing was broken fleet-wide between\n> 2026-08-23 and 2026-08-27. That outage is over. Measured today (2026-09-01), this repository's\n> last three scheduled release runs all succeeded, and the published version on npm matches the\n> current release:\n> \n> - release workflow: 2026-08-29 success, 2026-08-30 success, 2026-08-31 success\n> - npm `latest`: 2026.8.31\n> \n> Nothing here needs a fix; the failing condition no longer exists. The auto-filed issue simply\n> has no counterpart step that closes it once the workflow recovers, so it stayed open for five\n> days after the cause was gone.\n>"
